    "body": "- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Issue\r\n\r\nWhen repositories configure Git diff filters in `.gitattributes` (for example, `git-crypt`), index blobs are stored in an encrypted/transformed format. Because `git show` on plain blobs does not apply text conversion filters by default, `mini.diff` receives raw unconverted binary/ciphertext as the reference text. Comparing this against the buffer's decrypted plain text results in false-positive diff hunks across the entire file, even when the repository is clean.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\n- Pass `--textconv` to `git show` when fetching reference text from the Git index in `H.git_set_ref_text`.\r\n- For files with diff filters defined in `.gitattributes`, Git executes the configured textconv filter before outputting content, providing `mini.diff` with matching plain text.\r\n- For standard files without diff filters, `git show --textconv` behaves identically to `git show`.\r\n\r\n#### Test data\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><b>Reproducibility Steps</b></summary>\r\n\r\n### 1. Generating Test Data (`git-crypt` repository)\r\n\r\nRun the following commands to create a clean, reproducible test repository with `git-crypt` configured:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nmkdir -p test-gitcrypt/content && cd test-gitcrypt\r\ngit init\r\ngit-crypt init\r\n\r\n# Configure clean/smudge and diff filters\r\necho \"content/** filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt\" > .gitattributes\r\n\r\ncat << 'EOF' > content/secrets.md\r\n# Confidential Project Notes\r\n\r\nThis file is encrypted using git-crypt.\r\nThe working tree is clean.\r\nMini.diff should compare against the decrypted index.\r\nEOF\r\n\r\ngit add .\r\ngit commit -m \"Add encrypted notes\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>",
