            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've looked into this a bit more and (as expected) this is not quite as simple. From `git help show`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n--textconv, --no-textconv\r\n   Allow (or disallow) external text conversion filters to  be  run  when\r\n   comparing  binary  files.  See  gitattributes(5)  for details. Because\r\n   textconv filters are typically a  one-way  conversion,  the  resulting\r\n   diff  is  suitable  for  human consumption, but cannot be applied. For\r\n   this reason, textconv filters are enabled by  default  only  for  git-\r\n   diff(1) and git-log(1), but not for git-format-patch(1) or diff plumb‐\r\n   ing commands.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI.e. it is not possible/safe to apply hunks for files in which `--textconv` actually matters. It *might* be okay to still show diff in such files, but not being able to apply needs to be documented.\r\n\r\nThere is also airblade/vim-gitgutter#796 for reference.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am not comfortable adding this before the (hopefully) upcoming release. Maybe after it and improved 'mini.diff' tests.",
